# Digi Ecosystem – root .gitignore

# Claude Code agent worktrees (ephemeral copies; do not commit)
.claude/worktrees/
/.worktrees/

# Local Claude Code overrides (tokens, paths — never commit)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Claude Code runtime state (scheduler lock, transient)
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# npm output at any depth. Deliberately NOT anchored: `npm ci` at the repo root
# materializes nested node_modules in any workspace whose dep version cannot be hoisted
# — package-lock.json carries such `apps/*/node_modules/...` entries today — and an
# anchored rule leaves those untracked. Coverage otherwise falls to each workspace
# shipping its own .gitignore; packages/design ships none, so this rule is its
# only cover.
node_modules/

# Next.js build output at any depth. Deliberately NOT anchored, for the same
# reason as node_modules/ above: coverage otherwise falls to each app shipping
# its own .gitignore, and a new app that does not (apps/digiquant-app on
# feat/dig-183 is the live example — it had to be added by hand after 0f193360
# committed its .next/dev tree) leaks the moment someone runs a build in it.
# A .next/dev tree carries Next-generated draft-mode and signing material, so
# committing it puts secrets in permanent history and forces a
# .gitleaks.toml allowlist entry to silence the scanner — an allowlist entry is
# the wrong instrument for build output. `.next-*` covers digichat, whose
# distDir is DIGICHAT_DIST_DIR (apps/digichat/next.config.ts) and is therefore
# not always literally `.next`.
.next/
.next-*/

# Agent session state (opencode session/storage/db files) — regenerated per
# machine, never shared. Unanchored for the same reason as the rules above: a
# worktree-local or nested checkout carries its own .opencode/.
# Matched by contents at any depth (`**/`), not just at the root: nested app
# trees carry their own .opencode/ too, and `apps/digichat/.opencode/` must stay
# ignored. Ignoring contents rather than the directory itself is what lets the
# exception below reach a file. Goals, memory, node_modules stay ignored.
**/.opencode/*
# Exception: the agent-runtime plugins are tracked code, not machine state.
# projects-path-guard.js is the projects/ read boundary (DIG-1302); a control
# that is not in every clone is not a control. Anchored to the root repo, so a
# nested app's .opencode/plugins/ stays ignored.
!/.opencode/plugins/

# Cloudflare Pages Functions for digithings.ai are authored under
# apps/digithings-web/functions/ and mirrored to a repo-root functions/ by
# scripts/build-digithings.sh at build time (CF requires functions/ at the project
# root). The generated copy is a build artifact — never commit it.
/functions/

.venv/
.venv-ci/
venv/
.env
.env*
projects/*/.env
# Agent-local secrets / scratch (vault keys, signup drafts) — never commit
.local/
config/dogfood-digiproject.local.yaml
docker-compose.override.yml

# Confidential: project configs and deployments (never share)
# Anchored to repo root so docs/projects/ (public dogfooding projects) is not captured.
# Allowlist projects/README.md only (private-repo pointer index).
/projects/*
!/projects/README.md
# Confidential: Counsel's client data and data protection policy (never share).
# Not source code, and not ours to extend this repository's MIT licence over —
# Counsel version-controls it as a Paperclip issue document on DIG-1502 instead.
# Anchored to repo root for the same reason as /projects/* above: an unanchored
# rule would also match docs/knowledge/, which scripts/seed_knowledge_vault.py
# uses as a real vault directory. The whole directory is ignored, not an allowlist
# of files, so what Counsel adds later is covered too.
# dt-snapshot's capture step (`git add -A`) honours this, which is what keeps the
# policy out of the backup refs it pushes to the public github remote.
# Pinned by tests/scripts/test_gitignore_knowledge_policy.py — DIG-1522.
/knowledge/
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.cache/

# Runtime results (exports, audit logs) – recreated on run
digiquant/results/

# Repo-root runtime caches (research price-history, agent-cache paths) — JAN-004
/data/

# Local agent memory archives (Cursor/agent tooling) — JAN-005
.remember/

# Local digikey dev SQLite (run_stack_local.sh) — JAN-006
.local_digikey.sqlite
/*.sqlite

# Dashboard static portfolio fallback — stop tracking after REM-037 (JAN-007)
apps/dashboard/public/dashboard-data.json

# digithings-web OpenAPI explorer assets (copied at prebuild / predev from
# docs/openapi/ + swagger-ui-dist — never commit the vendored copies).
apps/digithings-web/public/openapi/
apps/digithings-web/public/swagger-ui/
# openwiki visualizer export (scripts/build-digithings.sh writes dist/openwiki
# on deploy; local preview generates the same tree under public/ so /openwiki works).
apps/digithings-web/public/openwiki/


# Secrets and credentials
.env*
projects/*/.env*
secrets.yaml
digikey/examples/vault.yaml

# Local stack (scripts/run_stack_local.sh)
.local_stack_pids
.litellm-local.log

# Log files
*.log

# Large data files and caches (CSV, Parquet, pickles)
# note: sample data in repo may be checked in intentionally, but user-owned
# datasets should not be
**/data/*.csv
**/data/*.parquet
**/data/*.pkl
**/data/*.pickle
**/data/*/*.csv
**/data/*/*.parquet
**/data/*/*.pkl
**/data/*/*.pickle

# Packaging output
digi-bundle-*.tar.gz
.DS_Store

# digigraph ECharts (installed in Docker / local npm ci; do not vendor node_modules)
digigraph/src/digigraph/tools/analytics/visualization/echarts/node_modules/

# digisearch EDGAR dev exports (generated; keep devdata/edgar_sample/.gitkeep)
digisearch/devdata/edgar_sample/edgar_*.md
digisearch/devdata/edgar_sample/edgar_*.yaml

# Local SQLite databases
*.sqlite

# Coverage artifacts
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml

# macOS
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Editor / tooling
.vscode/
.idea/
*.bak

# DesignSync local tooling output (node_modules, bundles, screenshots, canvases — generated)
.ds-sync/
ds-bundle/
canvases/

# Strategy calibrations — proprietary tuning values
**/calibrations.json
# SDCA BTC power-law coefficients: the real fit
# (strategies/sdca/btc_power_law_coefficients.json) IS committed as of #3173 —
# it is a public model (window + source in `notes`), unlike calibrations.json.
# The synthetic btc_power_law_coefficients.example.json placeholder stays as
# the load_coefficients() fallback when the real file is absent. Do not
# gitignore the real file.
# Strategy Pine files embed calibrated inputs (input.int(70, ...)) — keep private.
# The indicator library (pinescript/indicators/*.pine) is calibration-free and is
# committed as reusable fallback code.
**/pinescript/*.pine

# Private client projects live under root /projects/* (anchored above) — never
# add an unanchored `projects/` rule here, it would also capture docs/projects/,
# which ADR-0006 reserves for public, committed dogfood projects.

# playwright-mcp scratch output (page snapshots, console logs)
.playwright-mcp/

# digiclaw scheduler durable state (local)
.digiclaw/
.deno/

# digivoice runtime data — model weights, recorded wavs, and the session
# history JSONL. The data directory lives outside the repo by default
# (~/Library/Application Support/digivoice on macOS, $XDG_DATA_HOME on Linux);
# these catch a DIGIVOICE_DATA_DIR pointed inside the tree.
**/ggml-*.bin
**/history.jsonl
**/recordings/*.wav

# Customer data artifacts (DIG-1498 R5, DIG-2607).
#
# `scripts/index_occ_tickets.py` writes full non-anonymized Zammad ticket
# bodies into the digisearch `occ_tickets` index — customer names, customer
# emails and internal-only staff notes, unmasked by design in demo mode. The
# retired `seed_occ_tickets` supervisor program wrote the same shape and was
# removed for it (see apps/digithings-stack-cloudflare/container/supervisor/
# supervisord.conf). Anything it produces is customer data, never source.
#
# Anchored on the file name so the real source scripts stay committable:
# `scripts/index_occ_tickets.py` does not begin with `occ_tickets`, and
# tests/scripts/test_gitignore_build_artifacts.py pins that.
occ_tickets/
occ_tickets*.json
occ_tickets*.jsonl
occ_tickets*.ndjson
seed_occ_tickets*
*_occ_tickets_snapshot*.json
